## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical, end-to-end thinking about GPU-backed perf testing, tail latency, and backpressure, not just theory.

## Key Concepts
- GPU utilization, memory pressure, kernel time
- Data transfer, batching, dynamic batching
- Queue depth, backpressure, warmup
- Mixed workloads and tail-latency targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// workload sampler (pseudo)
function sampleBatchSize() {
  const r = Math.random();
  if (r < 0.5) return 1;
  if (r < 0.8) return 2;
  if (r < 0.95) return 4;
  return 8;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you isolate GPU bottlenecks when data transfer saturates the PCIe link?
- What changes to your plan if the model is quantized to int8 and batching latency changes?

